{title: What Child Is This}
{key: Am}
{time: 6/8}

{start_of_verse: 1}
What [Am]Child is [C]this who, [G]laid to [Em]rest on [Am]Mary's [F]lap is [E7]slee[**]ping?
Whom [Am]Angels [C]greet with [G]anthems [Em]sweet, while [Am]shepherds [E7]watch are [Am]kee[**]ping?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C]This, [**]this is [G]Christ the [Em]King, whom [Am]shepherds [F]guard and [E7]Angels [**]sing
[C]Haste, [**]haste, to [G]bring Him [Em]laud, the [Am]Babe, the [E7]Son of [Am]Ma[**]ry.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Why [Am]lies He [C]in such [G]mean [Em]estate, where [Am]ox and [F]ass are [E7]fee[**]ding?
Good [Am]Christians, [C]fear, for [G]sinners [Em]here The [Am]silent [E7]Word is [Am]plea[**]ding.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: 3}
So [Am]bring Him [C]incense, [G]gold and [Em]myrrh, come [Am]peasant, [F]king to [E7]own [**]Him
The [Am]King of [C]kings sal[G]vation [Em]brings, let [Am]loving [E7]hearts en[Am]throne [**]Him.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
